{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact b070ffbffd814ab9cea091b222ddeee77f46be99, all 35 changed paths versus main 6477b73, S5 results note first. Reviewed in a separate detached checkout: npm ci, npm ci --prefix experiments/pds, npm run check (0), npm run test:flows -- --group evolution (25/25), npm test (267/267, 0 skipped), tree clean afterwards. All 88 sourceHashes in each of evolution.json, evolution-runtime.json, participation.json and host-flows.json match HEAD; all 21 profile sources match and the engine CID is unchanged.\n\nBoth required changes of verdict c2e51e2d are closed as filed. The activation now freezes exactly the signed closure blocks, loads the candidate only from that isolated bundle, and converts every available loader or view failure to invalid_activation while missing or corrupt named bytes still pause; the new regressions pin an incomplete and an in-bound extra closure to identical projections on a full and a closure-only reader with following entries, and the query-less Inlay MissingError case. A mutant restoring the old load through the whole reader and a mutant rethrowing non-InterpretationErrors each turn their regression red. My reader-parity probes agree on every in-bound case: missing file, extra unrelated CID, omitted root, foreign codec, ghost manifest dependency, valid candidate, and a block corrupt on one reader only pausing only that reader.\n\nOne required change remains, in the same category the first review named. A signed closure whose blocks are each available and each within 512 KiB, but whose total exceeds the 512 KiB CAR bound, is judged on the host and never delivered to the client. Host: readSource succeeds for every closure CID, SourceBundle.collect throws definition_size inside the try at src/definition/activation.ts lines 40 to 50, and invalid_activation is recorded with the next entry effective. Sync: src/host/application.ts lines 120 to 121 run the same collect, swallow the failure and omit the candidate. Client: the worker and CLI never receive the closure and pause at N with content_missing on every sync, permanently. Reproduced with two staged bundles of about 300 KiB each and a closure mixing them: host outcomes invalid_activation then effective; sync candidate omitted with definition_size; client stalled at position 1 with content_missing and no outcomes; the same log without the extra block is effective on both. This contradicts docs/evolution.md lines 29 to 31 and the note's \"deterministically invalid on both readers\", and the new regression cannot catch it because its extra CID fits within the bound. Fix: make the verdict computable from data both verifiers can obtain, for example by delivering closure blocks in sync up to the pool bound rather than the definition bound and letting the candidate load enforce the size deterministically on both sides, or by refusing over-bound closures before any reader is consulted; add a regression whose closure exceeds 512 KiB and asserts identical projections on the full and closure-only readers.\n\nNon-blocking, take up in the same pass. The closure equality check at activation.ts lines 44 to 45 is dead after the isolated load, since load already refuses a missing manifest file and an extra bundle block; delete it. The documented CLI expected field for compare and stage is exercised only through the definition alias; switch the gate's stage call to expected. Converting every non-incompatible error inside the try to a durable invalid_activation means a transient host fault such as an out-of-memory during evaluate becomes a permanent verdict another verifier will not reproduce; say so in docs/evolution.md as the accepted trade-off. The S5 screenshots were not regenerated for this head. The S3 retained evidence still names superseded hashes for its own subject files; \"historical until S6\" is a label, not a refresh. ApplicationHost.restore still aborts every app on the first old-profile app and is never called by scripts/serve.ts.\n\nArchitecture: definition and runtime layers only; the isolated-bundle boundary is the right place and the profile CID pins it. Security: the remaining verifier divergence is reachable only by a granted key, but it converts a grantee's mistake into a permanent client pause the host does not share, which is the class the previous verdict required closed. Simplification: remove the dead closure comparison. Nothing here adopts the plan-review recommendations.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:2aee66fccc4e7ae45f4a208ad2138880dfa3f2df","head":"b070ffbffd814ab9cea091b222ddeee77f46be99","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:b83ef46bb92a7801db51dbd5877bb2a13a14ab42\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:a6df2c50e05145f10805b036a020294bfb6de7f1","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}